@ch_alpha:I{ky=~2:al;pr=@project;so=[@ref_a,@ref_b,@measure];st=observed;vl=binary;wh=@actor;wy=~132:Measured: zero fractional-alpha pixels in either reference. Observation from two placeholder files, not a stated compositing policy.}
@ch_canvas:I{ky=~2:px;pr=@project;so=[@brief,@ref_a,@ref_b];st=unresolved;vl=?;wh=@user;wy=~285:The user stated the final canvas size is not chosen. Both references are 32x32 with an 18x25 occupied area, which is evidence of intent but not a decision. The choice is coupled to edge_treatment: a 2px rim is not viable below roughly 48px of canvas for two distinguishable characters.}
@ch_edges:I{ky=~14:edge_treatment;pr=@project;so=[@brief,@ref_a,@ref_b,@measure];st=conflict;vl=[~68:continuous 2px dark outline in #25354A, as supplied in reference.png,~72:no outline; flat single-color silhouette, as supplied in reference-b.png];wh=@user;wy=~455:The user named this disagreement explicitly. Measured: the two files share an identical 390-cell silhouette and differ in exactly 180 pixels, every one of them #25354A in reference.png against #56B5BC in reference-b.png. The rim is a uniform 2 cells deep and spends 46.2% of the character's pixels on its own edge. A third option, a 1px rim at 92 cells, is offered in the decision study but has not been put to the user. Unresolved until the user chooses.}
@ch_engine:I{ky=~6:engine;pr=@project;so=[@brief];st=unresolved;vl=?;wh=@user;wy=~136:No target engine or import route was stated. Engine acceptance for the family cannot be planned concretely or verified until one exists.}
@ch_light:I{ky=~2:li;pr=@project;so=[@ref_a,@ref_b];st=unresolved;vl=?;wh=@user;wy=~132:Both references are flat fills with no shading, so they establish no light direction. Side-view characters normally need one stated.}
@ch_palette:I{ky=~2:pl;pr=@project;so=[@ref_a,@ref_b,@measure];st=observed;vl=[~7:#56B5BC,~7:#25354A,~7:#F4DDA2];wh=@actor;wy=~248:Measured across both references: teal fill, navy rim, cream marks. Observation only. Whether these are the final character colors or placeholder colors has not been stated, and #25354A exists only in the outline treatment that is still in conflict.}
@ch_roles:I{ky=~12:family_roles;pr=@project;so=[@brief];st=confirmed;vl=[~5:scout,~5:medic];wh=@user;wy=~69:The user named a scout and a medic as the two members of this family.}
@ch_sampling:I{ky=~2:sa;pr=@project;so=[];st=proposed;vl=nearest;wh=@actor;wy=~164:Proposed for a side-view pixel game whose references are hard-edged and unantialiased. Not confirmed; it depends on the unresolved display_scale and engine choices.}
@ch_scale:I{ky=~13:display_scale;pr=@project;so=[@brief];st=unresolved;vl=?;wh=@user;wy=~198:Not in the brief. The decision study shows the three outline treatments are nearly indistinguishable at 1x and clearly different at 8x, so this choice materially affects the edge_treatment decision.}
@ch_view:I{ky=~2:vw;pr=@project;so=[@brief];st=confirmed;vl=side;wh=@user;wy=~128:The user stated a side-view game. The references are front-facing and therefore do not establish the production view themselves.}
