@v_study_decide:V{at=~25:2026-09-11T00:00:00+00:00;ev=[@e_study_decide];rq=@q_study_decidable;st=pass;tk=@study_edges;wh=@actor;wy=~426:Viewed the contact sheet and the dark-ground crop as images. All three treatments appear on light, dark and busy grounds at native scale, x4 and x8; the report names a weakest cell per treatment and those cells are the ones that actually look weakest. The sheet carries no printed row labels, so it is decidable beside the report rather than alone: recorded as a limitation, not a failure. This does not choose edge_treatment.;xr=@x_study}
@v_study_repro:V{at=~25:2026-09-11T00:00:00+00:00;ev=[@e_study_repro];rq=@q_study_repro;st=pass;tk=@study_edges;wh=@actor;wy=~450:Re-ran work/tools/edge_study.py: measurement.json, the contact sheet and all three variant PNGs regenerate byte-identically from the two supplied references. work/tools/verify_study.py then recomputed 34 claims from the PNGs alone, independently of measurement.json, and matched each against the literal report text: 34 pass, 0 fail, including both input digests, the 390-cell silhouette, the 180 differing pixels and the 92/82/58 ring depth profile.;xr=@x_study}
